From d42790d7658141bc6bb1e249721b95fe261f067f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:44:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(landing): sunrise hero and a sticker tray that obeys
 gravity

The hero is now a full-bleed cobalt sky with a die-cut sun rising from
behind the paper the rest of the page is printed on. The About section
gets a release-liner tray the stickers drop into under real gravity.

Hero
- studio/hero/: a paper-cut scene built from real CSS depth. Flat cobalt
  bands, a ring of rays, a far hill, the sun as six ink cut-outs under its
  painted face (so it shows an edge when it tilts), clouds, four stickers
  and the paper ground. No WebGL, no images, no new dependencies.
- use-hero-scene: one rAF loop for pointer parallax and scroll, running
  only while the hero is on screen. Touch gets scroll only.
- The title takes a stepped ink edge, the primary action turns butter, and
  the entrance waits for the Sticker Boot to lift.
- Nothing loops forever: the sun rises, three rings leave it, sparkles
  twinkle and stickers drift a few times, then the hero is still.

Gravity
- studio/gravity/physics.ts: a small rigid-circle world (spin, contact
  friction, walls, floor, sleep), pure and unit-tested.
- pit-runtime.ts: releases the stickers when the tray scrolls into view,
  lets you pick one up and fling it, shake the tray, and sleeps at rest.
- sticker-pit.tsx: the tray, two new round stamps, and a real "Shake the
  tray" button. Reduced motion shows each sticker in its own outline.
- The hero's stickers fall into the tray and leave dashed outlines.

Cleanup
- The journey now flies only the sun and the heart; the hero-to-About
  flyers, their docks and the old hero-art scroll block are removed along
  with the dead hero CSS.
- docs/HERO_SUNRISE_GRAVITY.md records the directions weighed.

Tests: 7 new physics tests; the journey runtime test now asserts the
sun and heart are the only flyers.
